We find the distance for all the points using the distance formula:
For (1,4)14(1,4): (1−0)2+(4−0)2=17superscript102superscript40217\sqrt{(1-0)^{2}+(4-0)^{2}}=\sqrt{17}
For (3,5)35(3,5): (3−0)2+(5−0)2=34superscript302superscript50234\sqrt{(3-0)^{2}+(5-0)^{2}}=\sqrt{34}
For (−6,0)60(-6,0): (−6−0)2+(0−0)2=36superscript602superscript00236\sqrt{(-6-0)^{2}+(0-0)^{2}}=\sqrt{36}
For (−4,−2)42(-4,-2): (−4−0)2+(−2−0)2=20superscript402superscript20220\sqrt{(-4-0)^{2}+(-2-0)^{2}}=\sqrt{20}
Therefore, the point farthest from the origin is (−6,0)60\boxed{(-6,0)}.
Final Answer: The final answer is (−6,0)60(-6,0). I hope it is correct.

